<meta name=3D"description" content=3D"Can you solve this real interview que=
stion? Task Scheduler - You are given an array of CPU tasks, each labeled w=
ith a letter from A to Z, and a number n. Each CPU interval can be idle or =
allow the completion of one task. Tasks can be completed in any order, but =
there's a constraint: there has to be a gap of at least n intervals between=
 two tasks with the same label.

Return the minimum number of CPU intervals required to complete all tasks.

&nbsp;

Example 1:

Input: tasks =3D [&quot;A&quot;,&quot;A&quot;,&quot;A&quot;,&quot;B&quot;,&=
quot;B&quot;,&quot;B&quot;], n =3D 2

Output: 8

Explanation: A possible sequence is: A -&gt; B -&gt; idle -&gt; A -&gt; B -=
&gt; idle -&gt; A -&gt; B.

After completing task A, you must wait two intervals before doing A again. =
The same applies to task B. In the 3rd interval, neither A nor B can be don=
e, so you idle. By the 4th interval, you can do A again as 2 intervals have=
 passed.

Example 2:

Input: tasks =3D [&quot;A&quot;,&quot;C&quot;,&quot;A&quot;,&quot;B&quot;,&=
quot;D&quot;,&quot;B&quot;], n =3D 1

Output: 6

Explanation: A possible sequence is: A -&gt; B -&gt; C -&gt; D -&gt; A -&gt=
; B.

With a cooling interval of 1, you can repeat a task after just one other ta=
sk.

